- * A mapped driver gets NULL DriverObject/RegistryPath, so it MUST NOT call
- * IoCreateDevice/IoCreateSymbolicLink. Instead it shares memory with user mode
- * through a named section and services requests from a polling system thread.
+ * The section is mapped into SYSTEM address space (MmMapViewInSystemSpace),
+ * never into a process's user address space: a user VA only exists while the
+ * address space of that specific process is active, so it must not be stored
+ * in a global and used from an arbitrary context.
