- * Shared buffer layout (user mode maps the same section):
- *   +0x000  KM_SHARED header (command/status/pid/address/size)
+ * DriverEntry must therefore run on a system thread (or any thread whose
+ * address space includes the system half, which is every thread). It must not
+ * be called on a user-process thread relying on that process's user VAs.
+ *
+ * Shared buffer layout (user mode maps the same section by name):
+ *   +0x000  KM_SHARED header (command/completion/pid/address/size)
  *   +0x400  data area (read results, write payloads, image path)
  *
  * Commands: 1 = read, 2 = write, 3 = image path.
+ *
+ * Protocol (single consumer, no lost commands):
+ *   client : write Pid/Address/Size, then Command = cmd
+ *   kernel : Command = 0 (atomic latch), process, ErrorCode, Completion++
+ *   client : waits for Completion != seq0; never writes Completion.
+ * Because the latch clears Command before dispatching, a command can never be
+ * executed twice, and a client that publishes while the kernel is busy cannot
+ * have its request silently discarded: it stays pending for the next pass.
